                  - [x] WPA  (WPA2/WPA3 passphrase; WEP omitted — broken since 2007, explained on the page)
                  - [x] and all the other types on https://randomkeygen.com/  (that site was rebuilt; the
                        catalogue follows its CURRENT generators — its old CodeIgniter/160-bit/504-bit/WEP
                        entries no longer exist there either)
            - [x] Napkin Math; A system for self-documenting back of the envelope style calculations
                  (DONE 2026-08-19 - plan Phase 8. Built as specified. Deviations, all recorded in
                   docs/dev/tools/napkin-math.md: MathLive's built-in text shortcuts are switched off
                   because they corrupt multi-letter variable names; an operator the generator has no
                   rule for is refused by name rather than emitted; and the generated code carries
                   rounding and modulo helpers where a language disagrees with the maths.)
                  - [x] Use Mathlive https://mathlive.io/mathfield/ for doing the entry, it will give you a parse tree you can get the variables with easily
                        - [x] You can find a svelte starting point here: https://mathlive.io/mathfield/guides/svelte/
                        - [x] The compute engine may be helpful: https://mathlive.io/compute-engine/
                        - [x] This does add some complications
                              - [x] There are several math operations that exist, you can use the MathML parsing to figure out which operation, but you will need more than just a basic add, multiply divide, etc.
                              - [x] The variable names will by default be split out into separate letters (e.g. `"count"` becomes `"c", "o","n","u","t"` which are not even in order sometimes). Below is a starter component that addresses this one way:
```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import "mathlive";
  import "https://esm.run/@cortex-js/compute-engine"
  import type {
    MathfieldElement,
    MathfieldElementAttributes
  } from "mathlive";

  type Props = {
    value?: string;
  } & Partial<MathfieldElementAttributes>;

  let { value = $bindable(), ...rest }: Props = $props();

  const config = {
    "smart-mode": true,
    "placeholder": "\\textbf{enter calculation}",
    "smart-fence": true
  };

  let data = $state("");

  function init(node: MathfieldElement) {
    /*
     * Turn sequences such as:
     *
     *   months
     *   count
     *   totalCount
     *   item_42
     *
     * into single MathLive symbols.
     */
    
    node.onInlineShortcut = (_mf, s) => {
      if (/^[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*$/.test(s)) {
        return `\\mathit{${s}}`;
      }

      return undefined;
    };

    if (value) {
      node.value = value;
    }

    const handleInput = () => {
      value = node.value;

      data = JSON.stringify(
        JSON.parse(node.getValue("math-json")),
        null,
        2
      );
    };

    node.addEventListener("input", handleInput);

    // Initialize
    data = JSON.stringify(
      JSON.parse(node.getValue("math-json")),
      null,
      2
    );

    return {
      destroy() {
        node.removeEventListener("input", handleInput);
      }
    };
  }
</script>

<math-field
  use:init
  {...rest}
  {...config}
></math-field>

<pre><code>{data}</code></pre>

<style>
  math-field {
    min-width: 50%;
  }

  pre {
    white-space: pre-wrap;
  }
</style>
```
